==Sanskrit==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|iir-pro|sa}} (compare Avestan {{term|tr=mātar|lang=ae}}, Old Persian {{term|𐎶𐎠𐎫𐎠|lang=peo|tr=mātā}}), from {{etyl|ine-pro|sa}} {{m|ine-pro|*méh₂tēr}} (compare Old Armenian {{term|մայր|lang=xcl|tr=mayr|sc=Armn}}, Ancient Greek {{term|μήτηρ|tr=mētēr|lang=grc}}, Old Church Slavonic {{term|мати|tr=mati|lang=cu}}, Latin {{term|mater|māter|lang=it}}, Old English {{m|ang|mōdor}} (> English {{term|mother|lang=en}}).

===Noun===
{{sa-noun|g=f|tr=mā́tṛ}}

# [[mother]]

